【3.8 Classification performance analysis · sec024-p2】Accuracy: Accuracy is an essential metric for the evaluation of the results of DL classifiers. It is a summary of the true positive and true negatives divided by the confusion of the matrix components’ total values. The most accurate model is an excellent one, but it is imperative to ensure that symmetric sets of data with almost equal false positive values and false negative values. Thus, the elements of the confusion matrix mentioned above will be calculated to evaluate the effectiveness of our proposed classification model for the COVID-19 database.

